# COPIED-METHOD-DECLARED-FORMAL, a static candidate through a callable formal: runs gives g the named Structure Wide
# itself (pad 9, x 4), a candidate the translation knows.  The class of the callable g holds admits it by its own
# model -- getq's Wide (4 + 1), getr's Other by name (40 + 1) -- and the class of getz, whose Zed asks z, refuses it
# where runs forms the input, as runs' implicit `implements`, which runs' handler takes (77); no other class's model is
# asked.  HEAD admitted to the contract (getr read Wide's first place: 91).  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
Wide:
    int: pad 9
    int: x 4
end: Wide
Other:
    int: x 5
end: Other
Zed:
    int: z 6
    int: x 7
end: Zed
fn: getq (Wide: q; int: k) int
    return: q\x + k
end: getq
fn: getr (Other: q; int: k) int
    return: q\x * 10 + k
end: getr
fn: getz (Zed: q; int: k) int
    return: q\z * 100 + k
end: getz
fn: runs (getq: g) int
    int: r 0
    r: g(Wide; 1)
    catch: implements ()
        r: 77
    ---
    return: r
end: runs
int: a runs(getq)
int: b runs(getr)
int: c runs(getz)
int: ok 7
if: a != 5 || b != 41 || c != 77
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
